{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water","id":1549787,"title":"Holy Water?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-03T17:57:34-07:00","id":1549787,"title":"Holy Water?","content":"I looked through Hunter's Hunted; couldn't find anything on Holy Water. So, is there holy water in V:tM?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://onthescreenreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/tumblr_os8vydyk3d1s1v3r1o2_540.gif?w=848&amp;h=353\" target=\"_blank\">https://onthescreenreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/tumblr_os8vydyk3d1s1v3r1o2_540.gif?w=848&amp;h=353<br /> <br /> <img width=\"540\" height=\"225\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://onthescreenreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/tumblr_os8vydyk3d1s1v3r1o2_540.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://onthescreenreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/tumblr_os8vydyk3d1s1v3r1o2_540.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://onthescreenreviews.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/tumblr_os8vydyk3d1s1v3r1o2_540.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T01:27:32-07:00","id":1549808,"title":"","content":"The exact rules seem to vary by edition. However, typically Holy Water counts the same as placing a cross, Bible, or other holy object against the vampire's body. In Revised this would be rolling one's True Faith against the vampire's Willpower with each success dealing a level of aggravated damage. I don't know what edition you are using, but most editions have some variant of the above procedure.<br /> <br /> If you don't want the person using the holy water to be the one whose Faith counts, I'd rule you can use the Faith of the person who originally blessed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T01:43:12-07:00","id":1549809,"title":"","content":"To be fair, genuine holy water (aka. blessed by someone with True Faith) is harder to come by than Unicorns...<br /> <br /> Also worth to check with your DM why does True Faith work in your campaign?<br /> Using a cross or belssing water is the extension of their Faith or the conduit for a Higher Power (like the Salubri's Blessing of the Name when they channel an Angel's power whom they share a Celestial Name)<br /> Or no Faith ivolved it is purely psychological - even a bit Mage-like reality adjustment - it works because both the Vampire and the one who uses it (or the whole world) belives it <i>should</i> work and really there is nothing behind it?<br /> Or just phychological? The Vampire heard all of his life as a human then as a vampire what should happen?<br /> <br /> Either case it is extremly rare to get <i>real</i> Holy Water","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-04-2025, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T21:02:32-07:00","id":1549859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549809#post1549809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, genuine holy water (aka. blessed by someone with True Faith) is harder to come by than Unicorns...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather specific view on what Holy Water is, and more based on games than on real world definitions.<br /> <br /> Holy water is holy because it was blessed by a priest, a person with the religious authority to do so. The faith os such priest either isn't relevant at all, or is only tangentially relevant.<br /> <br /> A catholic character with True Faith wouldn't go around blessing water unless they're a Reverend, nor would doubt the ability of other Reverends to bless water for a single second. That's simply how the theology goes. There are exceptions (saints and, to a lesser extend, the Blessed), but a true believer would hardly think of themselves one such exception.<br /> <br /> So I'd mostly go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Black Fox</a>'s take on it: the person using the Holy Water uses their True Faith, if any, because their belief in its properties is the main thing going on. I'd accept the idea of someone with TF making Holy Water that always works, but that would be harder, akin to creating any other sort of Blessed item.<br /> <br /> &quot;Psychological&quot; effects are already baked into the game as Flaws. Vampires are definitely <b>not</b> affected by religious symbols, unless the individual vampire has one such weakness. Regular Holy Water, that finds common use in many rites and ceremonies, shouldn't affect vampires by default.<br /> <br /> For those who do want vampires to be more readily affected by faith and religion, I'd suggest to read Demon the Fallen and take inspiration there. Demons are, by design, far more affected by faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T21:48:34-07:00","id":1549862,"title":"","content":"Welcome back Monteparnas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T00:15:54-07:00","id":1549863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549859#post1549859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a rather specific view on what Holy Water is, and more based on games than on real world definitions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> Because the question was: is there holy water in V:tM?<br /> <br /> There is holy water in V:tM, but it is not from a local church, nor from a holy water vendor machine (fun fact, Greek inventor and mathematician Heron of Alexandria\u200b\u200b, invented the first vending machine which dispensed holy water after you put in a coin used in Egyptian temples to dispense water for ritual washings\u200b. Today you can have your own <b>Automatic Touchless Holy Water Dispenser </b>for around 400$) <br /> The person using the Holy Water uses their True Faith of course is logical to use his own Faith and power to bless the water before using, but that is basically what I said, just eliminated a middle man. <br /> My point still stands, in the World of Darkness finding genuine holy water (aka. blessed by someone with True Faith) is hard.<br /> You said you'd accept the idea of someone with TF making Holy Water that always works, but that would be harder, akin to creating any other sort of Blessed item.<br /> <br /> You are literally saying what I said...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T17:40:14-07:00","id":1549885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549863#post1549863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are literally saying what I said...</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to disagree, although we're mostly (but not just) discussing semantics here.<br /> <br /> You're choosing to define holy water as &quot;water that is capable of harming vampires by itself&quot;. I'm defining it as &quot;water that would be called holy by people within the setting, regardless if it harms vampires or not&quot;.<br /> <br /> But this difference is relevant because, more often than not, the holy water used to try and harm vampires will not be capital B Blessed by the game's standards, and we need to know if common holy water works in any way.<br /> <br /> A character with True Faith is capable of harming vampires with common holy water, so it is still holy water for the purposes of the question, even though it isn't within your definition.<br /> <br /> The only question that remains is: the holy water used by a True Faith character must be really blessed by a priest, or the character belief that it is holy is enough? The game never went into the details if a True Faith user must brandish genuine (but low case) holy paraphernalia, or if they can do with things they <i>think</i> will work, like the many false relics on the market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T19:28:28-07:00","id":1549889,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that there is holy water that exists because some folks have the strong true faith merit and imbued items throughout the ages.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall that Moncada's haven was filled with shrines that had true faith flowing from them that made visitors uncomfortable and his write up gave him a true faith merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T09:11:14-07:00","id":1549910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549889#post1549889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that there is holy water that exists because some folks have the strong true faith merit and imbued items throughout the ages.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall that Moncada's haven was filled with shrines that had true faith flowing from them that made visitors uncomfortable and his write up gave him a true faith merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019re right, but I\u2019m also deeply troubled by the idea of giving someone as unpleasant as Moncada True Faith. It sort of sounds like God is endorsing the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also firmly believe that regardless of what canon says, the Shadow Inquisitors from Dark Ages: Inquisitor are primarily powered by Numina, not True Faith, so I could be biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 04-07-2025, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T09:56:02-07:00","id":1549913,"title":"","content":"Even disregarding DA Inquisitor, the books have very consistently pointed out that the True Faith merit is not restricted to a specific religion or belief system. Nor is it restricted to people we as players would consider &quot;good.&quot; Considering a nasty character having True Faith an &quot;endorsement&quot; from the Lord OOC is ignoring the WoD's entire conceptualization of True Faith across the entire history of the game.<br /> <br /> And this only really matters because people are equating holy water and True Faith in the first place. Most vampire fiction just has holy-to-Christians items harm vampires on some level. VtM doesn't work that way. Symbols of faith by themselves have no power in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T10:52:21-07:00","id":1549917,"title":"","content":"In his write up Moncada's faith was always sincere and even becoming a member of the Lasombra clan didn't change it and he saw it as serving God's will. It grew darker and more twisted but it never wavered and maybe it grew even stronger and it's how he got the True Faith merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T12:59:47-07:00","id":1549920,"title":"","content":"Any rules as written are likely to only partly emulate whatever vampire trope you want. So some players may be dissatisfied with a canon answer. They want something more in tune with actual religious significance or better emulates literary, cinematic, or folkloric tropes. In that case, they can make whatever changes they need.<br /> <br /> Items that are blessed can be used by those without Faith provided the blessed items retain their sacral quality for a time dependent on the # of successes of True Faith role. That can be anytime between one round to permanent. Such items are considered to have a TF rating of one. Thus an ST could decide that holy water (or whatever) retains its quality for a certain amount of time, and thus can be treated accordingly despite the person using it not having True Faith of their own. The ST would just need to determine how long these items retain its quality.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, in addition to people having True Faith, the game also has many places that have their own True Faith ranking to reflect how people - particularly devout congregants - see that place as holy ground. Such holy ground typically does not affect the vampire in and of itself, but does add its True Faith rating to the person attempting to use TF against the vampire. Thus holy ground itself can ward and prevent vampires from entering, forcing the vampire to avoid it.<br /> <br /> So it would not be out of line if an ST wanted to use that kind of rule to determine the sacral quality of certain items instead of the actual user (or perhaps the consecrator). If the expectation is that the holy water, eucharist, or any other blessed or sacred item in and of itself has the power of True Faith, then the ST could assign that to them - effectively giving the user a higher rating of TF than they would normally have. Thus even people without True Faith might indeed be able to utilize it. To a Catholic who believes the sacramental bread is truly the body of Christ, that might be TF 5, 8, or some other number. To someone who believes it is just symbolic, maybe that falls to just 1, and to a non-believer it is zero. Holy water would probably be lower than the eucharist, but still as high as whatever the ST thinks would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Of course, now the ST has the responsibility of deciding what level of True Faith of each item has, determine by what means those items might lose their sacral quality (most often these kind of things need to be properly handled and kept isolated lest they become &quot;ordinary&quot;) and perhaps keep track of all kinds of things that might impact it. Respectfully handling holy water in a vial by a priest is one thing. But what about the same handling by a layman? What about the Frog brothers putting it in a supersoaker water gun? Does it decline in TF ranking or even end completely? For some STs it will be worth the work to figure out these things, but for others it'll be easier to default to the original version. It really depends on what the ST wants for their game and the expectations of the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549910#post1549910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you\u2019re right, but I\u2019m also deeply troubled by the idea of giving someone as unpleasant as Moncada True Faith. It sort of sounds like God is endorsing the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never liked the idea that vampires can have True Faith and don't have that in my own chronicles. I simply rule that vampires, being Damned, simply have a spiritual pollution that prevents them from accessing any power like that. Even if I wanted to include that in a chronicle, I certainly would not have someone like Moncada be able to utilize it. Not only does his behavior not align with what I would expect, his participation in the Sabbat would preclude it as the Sabbat can essentially be seen as a blasphemous parody of Christianity. You can't mock Christ and then receive his grace.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T13:43:02-07:00","id":1549921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549917#post1549917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In his write up Moncada's faith was always sincere and even becoming a member of the Lasombra clan didn't change it and he saw it as serving God's will. It grew darker and more twisted but it never wavered and maybe it grew even stronger and it's how he got the True Faith merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Moncada is REALLY dark and twisted. I can\u2019t imagine a just and loving God favoring him with True Faith.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> like I said in my original post, I don\u2019t really care what the canon answer is. I understand that White Wolf\u2019s interpretation of True Faith may differ from mine. I would never allow someone like Moncada to have True Faith, for the reasons <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> specifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:45:13-07:00","id":1549927,"title":"","content":"The problem with going on about not liking the official answer, is that we're not talking about getting together and having a game of VtM and figuring out if we want to change things, we're talking about the game itself; where the official answers matter (even if the thread is about changing them) because it's what avoids threads just being everyone shouting their opinions at each other.<br /> <br /> Like, do you want to have a discussion on whether the WoD can exist if it contains a truly just and truly loving supreme deity in it? Care to explain all the other evil shit that happens in the WoD that this being allows to happen? The problem of evil is perhaps the most discussed topic in all of philosophy, and that's in our world where damned vampires aren't an objectively real thing. A lot of the refutations of the problem of evil aren't going to survive contact with the reality of the WoD, and those that do aren't exactly great for the idea that a supreme deity wouldn't empower Moncada (a lot of them wholly embrace that divinely caused evil/suffering are necessary for the ultimate success of good).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:55:13-07:00","id":1549928,"title":"","content":"Philosophy is a great debate topic and I like reading about it and especially if it covers characters from popular culture like Batman, Transformers and Sun Zhu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T15:57:19-07:00","id":1549929,"title":"","content":"Moncada is not the only Kindred with the True Faith merit and I recall that the Ravnos Etienne had it and it was the only thing that made him survive being near the city of Acre when most of his kind would suffer final death or great agony if they got to close.<br /> <br /> The temporal minded kindred mocked him that he claimed domain over a city that he couldn't enter, but the wiser and more religious respected the fact that he could be that close. Why certain types have the true faith merit will probably never be really answered to anybodys satisfaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-07-2025, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T16:43:20-07:00","id":1549982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549910#post1549910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you\u2019re right, but I\u2019m also deeply troubled by the idea of giving someone as unpleasant as Moncada True Faith. It sort of sounds like God is endorsing the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also firmly believe that regardless of what canon says, the Shadow Inquisitors from Dark Ages: Inquisitor are primarily powered by Numina, not True Faith, so I could be biased.</div> </div> </div> </div>True Faith within the game is about truly being faithful, not about having faith in something that's true. Anyone can have True Faith as long as that means the character is, well, a zealot to be sincere. People of any faith can have True Faith and it has nothing to do with their gods backing their actions.<br /> <br /> In addition to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said about having a common ground for discussion (we can only debate the game if we start from the common ground of canon), I'd add that distinguishing faiths through rules, as in gatekeeping TF behind &quot;the favored by the True God&quot;, is extremely problematic. <b>Even</b> if your game has an objectively true religion, which is something I'm also very adamantly against. It seriously limits how players engage the game, the kinds of characters they'll build and how they'll roleplay those characters.<br /> <br /> Specific faiths may be better represented in rules terms by Numina than TF, but there's a world of difference between doing that just for mechanical concerns and doing that because only one is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T18:19:56-07:00","id":1549987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549929#post1549929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moncada is not the only Kindred with the True Faith merit and I recall that the Ravnos Etienne had it and it was the only thing that made him survive being near the city of Acre when most of his kind would suffer final death or great agony if they got to close.<br /> <br /> The temporal minded kindred mocked him that he claimed domain over a city that he couldn't enter, but the wiser and more religious respected the fact that he could be that close. Why certain types have the true faith merit will probably never be really answered to anybodys satisfaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not against Kindred in general having True Faith. I\u2019m against Moncada having True Faith. He is evil with a capital E. No mainstream religion and very few alternative religions would regard Moncada as a good person.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> In a nutshell, my WoD worldview postulates that the One revered by the Celestial Chorus is the source of True Faith. The good news is, I think WoD canon hews much closer to your view than mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T21:53:13-07:00","id":1549992,"title":"","content":"Christian theology would argue that even evil beings serve God's will and Moncada is a firm believer in that idealogy. I seem to recall that in his mind that God has made him part of the damned and he intends to fulfill that mandate. He might be mentally ill in some measure and maybe that is what is empowering him.<br /> <br /> Alas it's just idle speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T16:45:46-07:00","id":1550125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1549808#post1549808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact rules seem to vary by edition. However, typically Holy Water counts the same as placing a cross, Bible, or other holy object against the vampire's body. In Revised this would be rolling one's True Faith against the vampire's Willpower with each success dealing a level of aggravated damage. I don't know what edition you are using, but most editions have some variant of the above procedure. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that; it should be based on the faith of the person that blessed it. Which page is that on in the old V:tM books('90's)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T17:18:27-07:00","id":1550131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549787-holy-water?p=1550125#post1550125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which page is that on in the old V:tM books('90's)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy water is specifically mentioned on page 24 of the original Hunter's Hunted, and page 66 of the Inquisition. The general rules of holy objects placed upon vampires doing damage is mentioned wherever the True Faith rules are mentioned, but holy water may or may not be specifically mentioned.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:22:30-07:00","id":1550147,"title":"","content":"On a purely thematic and mechanical level (leaving aside all theology) I feel that True Faith in the World of Darkness should be limited to those who Do Not have access to the full power of a \u2018splat\u2019 - mostly because Kindred, Garou, Changelings et al already have Supernatural Power at their beck and call (Sometimes immense supernatural power), partly because to my mind True Faith works best when it pits heartfelt conviction against the aforesaid Supernatural Power (because doing so when you are a squishy mortal and they are very, very much <i>not</i> is the perfect definition of Faith seeking to move mountains).<br /> <br /> Whether this means True Faith should be denied the likes of ghouls and kinfolk as well is an interesting question (As is the question of whether belief in a Higher Power requires genuine, adamantine conviction when you not only have personal experience of phenomenal, cosmic powers in action - sometimes even on your behalf - but reliable access to supernatural powers all your own*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *That, however, is a philosophical question and I most definitely don\u2019t want to see this thread end in the next Great Schism - not least since the last ones were never all that great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}